+/*
+ Every synthesized event goes through one queue. testmanagerd performs one gesture at a time (a second
+ one fails with "only one gesture can be performed at a time") and reports each done about 200 ms after
+ its last finger lifts, so events from different clients (an agent's tap, a viewer's touches, typing)
+ must wait their turn instead of failing. Touches given as points (enqueueTouch:) that pile up while a
+ gesture runs are merged into one record, one finger after another, so they share that ~200 ms.
+ */
